    "background_story": "Baker was a talented but reclusive novelist who lived in a small, rural town. He spent most of his days holed up in his cabin, pouring his thoughts and emotions onto paper. Despite his success, Baker felt disquieted by the darkness that lurked within his own mind. His writing often explored the human condition, delving into themes of isolation and the blurred lines between reality and madness. As the years went by, Baker's stories became increasingly unsettling, reflecting the turmoil that churned within him. His fans were drawn to the eerie and haunting quality of his work, but few knew the true extent of Baker's inner struggles. The more he wrote, the more he felt like he was exorcising his own demons, yet the sense of disquiet never truly left him.",
